# DATA.md — Where data comes from

All data lives in JSON files in `data/`. Only `lib/db.js` reads or writes them,
so every other file just calls its functions.

| File | Holds |
|---|---|
| `data/products.json` | 28 laptops and computers |
| `data/users.json` | users (passwords are hashed) |
| `data/orders.json` | orders |
| `data/sessions.json` | signed-in sessions |

## Every query

| # | Query | Where | Key / URL | Refresh rule | Why |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Product list, product detail | Server (page) | `getProducts()`, `getProductBySlug()` | Fresh on every request | Public pages, good for SEO, no loading spinner |
| 2 | Orders list, order detail | Server (page) | `getOrdersFor(session.id)`, `getOrderFor(session.id, id)` | Fresh on every request | Private data, always scoped to the signed-in user |
| 3 | **Order status** (live) | Client, SWR | `/api/orders/[id]/status` | **Polled every 5 seconds**, stops when `delivered` or `cancelled` | The status changes while the user is watching |
| 4 | **Product search** (live) | Client, SWR | `/api/products?q=...&category=...` | **Debounced 400 ms**, no polling | Avoids one request per keystroke |

## How the two live queries start without a spinner

Both are **seeded with server data**:
- The page loads the data on the server and passes it as `initialProducts` /
  the first status.
- SWR uses it as `fallbackData`, so the first paint already has content.
- Search only calls the API after the user types something different from the
  starting search.

## Writes

| Action | Route | What changes |
|---|---|---|
| Place order | `POST /api/orders` | Adds an order, lowers stock |
| Cancel order | `POST /api/orders/[id]/cancel` | Sets status `cancelled`, puts stock back |

After a write, the page calls `router.refresh()` so the server data is read again.

## Cart

The cart is not in the database. It lives in React context and is saved in the
browser's `localStorage`. At checkout only product ids and quantities are sent.

## Known limit

JSON files cannot be written on Vercel (read-only disk). Locally everything
works. Before a real deployment only `lib/db.js` needs to change to a hosted
store. No other file would change.